languages/sample.md:3:13: placeholder-noun: "a name" is a placeholder; name the kind of name, such as "an identifier" or "a field name"
languages/sample.md:3:20: personified-verb: "The case" is not a person or a program and cannot "say"; make the program or person that acts the subject, or use a verb such as "holds", "marks", "declares" or "determines"
languages/sample.md:3:25: placeholder-noun: "what it is" is a free relative clause; name the exact term instead, such as "the element type" or "the verb's symbol"
languages/sample.md:3:30: self-reference: the sentence ends on "it is", which points back at its own subject "The case of a name"; end on the new fact instead
